t030o41-review2-verify-c: rc=1 (read from the .rc file; the harness notification reported
exit 0, which was the trailing `echo`'s status). Two FAIL lines, both explained, neither a
failure to reproduce a pass-C claim:

1. "F3 identity unchanged under CDPATH=." got an EMPTY identity. vf_snapshot itself fails
   under an exported CDPATH=. when given a relative spec path: its `cd "$spec" && pwd -P`
   consults CDPATH and prints the directory into the substitution. That fails closed (no
   identity, so no capture and no reuse in that environment) and is recorded as a
   measurement. It does not weaken F3 as a regression: `bash tests/shellcheck.sh` fails
   under CDPATH=. (rc=2) where the pre-repair command passes (rc=0), and a BASH_ENV file
   setting an unexported CDPATH fails it too (rc=2).

2. "live worktree unchanged" FAIL: the invoker copied the two review reports
   (t030o41-review2-passC.md, t030o41-review2-passD.md) into this directory while the
   script ran. Recomputed after the run, the live `git status --porcelain -uall -z` digest
   with exactly those two entries (and this run's own .rc) removed is 82131a3c...,
   equal to the digest taken before the run. No other live path changed.

Every other line passed: F3 (regression vs the pre-repair command; BASH_ENV decides the
command; a BASH_ENV-defined function runs inside the capture harness's own
`bash -o pipefail -c`) and F4 (with an absolute GIT_INDEX_FILE the suite passes and
rewrites that foreign index with fixture paths; the copy's own index is untouched).
